# Memories

A memory is one thing every agent working in this repository has to know
before it does anything: a name, a standing instruction from the user, a
convention that is not visible from the files. `CLAUDE.md` tells every
session to read this folder first.

A memory is short. It states the thing, says who decided it and when, and
says how to act on it. It is not a record of work done. That belongs in the
[ledger](../ledger/index.hmd). It is not a plan either.

| Document | Read | Holds |
|---|---|---|
| Memory | by every session, before anything else | what must be known to work here at all |
| Story | when asking what the project is for | the invention and where it stands |
| Ledger | when asking how it got here | one entry for each committed change |

## Naming

A memory is one file, named `SLH-M-NNNN-short-name.hmd`. `NNNN` is the next
free number, and a number is never reused.

## Rules

- A memory is written when the user says something that is meant to hold
  from now on, or asks for it to be remembered.
- One memory holds one thing.
- When the user changes their mind, the memory is edited to say the new
  thing, with the date. A memory that no longer holds is deleted, and its
  number is not reused.
- An agent does not write a memory from its own conclusions. If it thinks
  something should be one, it asks the user.

## The memories

| Memory | Holds |
|---|---|
| [SLH-M-0001](SLH-M-0001-project-name-and-nomenclature.hmd) | The project is called SLH, and how its documents are named |
| [SLH-M-0002](SLH-M-0002-project-memories-come-first.hmd) | This folder is the primary memory, and an agent's private memory is secondary |
